Collabora Online WOPI host for Tryton
=====================================

This module exposes a WOPI host for one binary field of one Tryton record.
It does not expose a file system, and consequently deliberately does not claim
support for relative-file operations.  `DeleteFile` clears the binary field.
`RenameFile` is available only if the binary field declares `filename`; it
updates that filename field and retains its extension.

Configuration
-------------

Add the following server configuration (the URLs must be the public HTTPS
URLs visible to the browser and to Collabora)::

    [collabora]
    url = https://office.example.com
    wopi_url = https://tryton.example.com
    wopi_secret = a-random-secret-with-at-least-32-bytes
    token_lifetime = 1800

`wopi_secret` must be stored in the server configuration or a secret manager,
never in the database.  Restrict the reverse proxy so only the Collabora
server can call `/<database>/wopi/`; TLS is mandatory in production.

Opening an editor
-----------------

Open this authenticated Tryton URL in a new browser tab::

    /<database>/collabora/open/<model>/<record>/<binary-field>?name=<filename>

The endpoint checks model, field and record rules, reads Collabora's discovery
document and posts to its versioned edit action.  It creates a short-lived,
HMAC-signed capability for exactly that binary field; the browser user never
supplies credentials to Collabora.  Set the URL action target to `new` in a
client integration.

The reusable `collabora_online.editor.get_editor_url()` function returns this
launch URL.  The module also adds the calculated `Edit URL` field to
`ir.attachment`; it is shown only for editable Collabora formats.

The host implements CheckFileInfo, GetFile, PutFile, DeleteFile, RenameFile
(where applicable), Lock, GetLock, RefreshLock, Unlock and UnlockAndRelock.
Permissions are rechecked on every WOPI callback, so a revoked Tryton
permission immediately stops access.
